    {
      "id": "9m9xVPUYOhwFGmWTL15K0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 508.0802001953126,
      "y": 1236.1666669999997,
      "width": 591.839599609375,
      "height": 325,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#e9ecef",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "ae",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1159202187,
      "version": 1966,
      "versionNonce": 385720523,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1792420978815,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Width goes in twice, same value: inside gray (for the output)\nand plain (for the input).\n\nInputs take a plain index because they're read only:\nmany threads reading one spot is harmless.\n`rgb[...]` works like any Rust slice.\n\nThe output takes only a ticket because many threads\nwrite at once, and two writing one spot would be a bug.\n`DisjointSlice` prevents that.\n\nThread thinks in (row, col); memory is flat,\nso every read and write is translated.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Width goes in twice, same value: inside gray (for the output)\nand plain (for the input).\n\nInputs take a plain index because they're read only:\nmany threads reading one spot is harmless.\n`rgb[...]` works like any Rust slice.\n\nThe output takes only a ticket because many threads\nwrite at once, and two writing one spot would be a bug.\n`DisjointSlice` prevents that.\n\nThread thinks in (row, col); memory is flat,\nso every read and write is translated.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
